### Module(s)

mini.snippets

### Description

I tried use using mini snippets, most languages worked fine when setting up snippets using gen_loader.from_lang, however, I noticed that snippets for files like typescriptreact, javascriptreact didn't work, I dug further into the docs and source code, I saw that you can lang_patterns to add snippets as provided in the example in the docs with latex.

local jsx_patterns = { "javascript.json", "react-es7.json" }
local tsx_patterns = { "typescript.json", "react-es7.json" }

local lang_patterns = {
	javascriptreact = jsx_patterns,
	typescriptreact = tsx_patterns,
}

local loader = gen_loader.from_lang({ lang_patterns = lang_patterns }),

snippets = {
    loader
}

However that didn't work either. I also tried inspecting the values to see if the snippets actually loaded, through print(vim.inspect(loader({ lang = 'javascriptreact' }))), which printed out the correct snippets. At this point I was really confused, then I accidentally pressed snippet expand when there was no available snippets and it notified me that the lang type was lang = tsx and lang = jsx instead of typescriptreact and javascriptreact, I ended up changing up the lang_patterns to use tsx and jsx and it finally worked

local lang_patterns = {
	jsx = jsx_patterns,
	tsx = tsx_patterns,
}

So my feature request would be, is it possible to make lang the same as the way filetypes work for most plugins, so for example using javascriptreact, and typescriptreact instead of tsx and jsx, most plugins and even neovim ftplugin uses this so I thought that would be case for this plugin as well which ended up causing me a lot of trouble setting up, almost gave up. Right now it doesn't work with friendly snippets or custom snippets if you have the snippet file named as javascriptreact and typescriptreact since mini snippets doesnt detect them as the correct language. I think this would make it easier and more intuitive to work with adding additional lang_pattern in the future for others and I. If thats not possible, could you add additional instructions to the docs regarding how to find the proper lang for different languages so lang_patterns dont get setup incorrectly, as I provided above expanding snippet when there are no matches gives information about the snippets which shows the language which is how I solved my problem, but not sure if thats the best solution.

ok that was a lot, but thanks for another amazing plugin, look forward to hearing back.
